<del></del></span> Best Frost Mage Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Frost Mage should typically use two passive trinkets, and sometimes one on-use and one passive, but rarely ever two on-use. In the case of Phase 5 of Mists of Pandaria, we will default to our two standard passive trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>There are no active trinkets of note worth mentioning for Frost Mage, as all of our strongest trinkets are Passive Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105540/kardris-toxic-totem">
<img alt="Kardris' Toxic Totem" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Kardris' Toxic Totem</span></a> is a very simple trinket, as it has an Intellect proc as its main benefit, and as its passive benefit it simply adds a chance to Multistrike and deal an additional 33% damage of the spell that triggered.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
