<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Frost Mages</span></h2>Every profession is relatively viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but engineering is always in somewhat of a class above due to the high quality of life tools it provides and safety net of nitro boosts. Tailoring also continues to be the best profession, especially due to its main ICD benefit being oftentimes re-applied with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Frost Mages</h4>Engineering has plenty of quality-of-life tools, such as repair bots, access to the bank in raids, an extra slow fall option and such, but the two main factors that make it so good for PVE are:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is an on-demand big main stat cooldown which can then be prolonged with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108978/alter-time">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_altertime.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alter Time</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> allows the player to escape mechanics that one would otherwise not be able to get out of, as well as helping correct major mistakes in positioning with far less of an uptime loss.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Frost Mages</h4>The main reason for getting tailoring is <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a>; this proc provides a fairly large amount of main stat, usually when most of your other cooldowns are also ongoing.<br/>As a bonus, you also get a far cheaper leg enchant with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125496/masters-spellthread">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_astralrecalgroup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Master's Spellthread</span></a>, since you don't have to buy the enchant from other players.<br/>Lastly, you can craft some BoE and BoP items that are useful at the start of the expansion. These aren't mandatory to obtain, but always nice to have the option to craft them.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
